 = \\dfrac{31!}{28!3!}$\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$\\dfrac{31!}{28!3!} = \\dfrac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1}$\n\nThe $28!$ terms cancel out, leaving us with:\n\n$\\dfrac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}$\n\nNow, let's evaluate the expression:\n\n$\\dfrac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\dfrac{29 \\times 31 \\times 30}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}$\n\n$= \\dfrac{29 \\times 31 \\times 15}{3}$\n\n$= \\dfrac{29 \\times 465}{3}$\n\n$= \\dfrac{13455}{3}$\n\n$= 4485$\n\nTherefore, $\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\boxed{4485}$.", "decode_seconds": 14.111029874067754, "draft_calls": 230, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 61, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "7ad23f549833b34cbe25e588ccd8cb6980306e33defce755cddb56206030da50", "method": "relay_candidate_1", "output_hash": "de8555487bff5ab3a29b039b18f1ee35d25e407d2f864b40f5268eafeb8d8301", "output_token_ids": [1271, 12849, 59060, 2042, 258, 316, 90, 2148, 15523, 1591, 32816, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 279, 15150, 369, 28559, 1473, 59836, 2042, 258, 316, 92462, 15523, 81, 92, 284, 1144, 67, 38118, 92462, 0, 15523, 81, 10509, 77, 3880, 42395, 32816, 271, 2940, 400, 77, 0, 3, 11105, 279, 54062, 315, 400, 77, 55976, 902, 374, 279, 2027, 315, 682, 6928, 26864, 709, 311, 400, 77, 3, 382, 644, 420, 1162, 11, 584, 617, 400, 77, 284, 220, 2148, 3, 323, 400, 81, 284, 220, 1591, 13244, 4815, 5451, 11, 1095, 596, 11294, 279, 8331, 10522, 1473, 72611, 0, 284, 220, 2148, 0, 284, 220, 2148, 1144, 15487, 220, 966, 1144, 15487, 220, 1682, 1144, 15487, 220, 1591, 1144, 15487, 220, 1544, 1144, 15487, 220, 1627, 1144, 15487, 220, 914, 1144, 15487, 220, 1187, 1144, 15487, 220, 1419, 1144, 15487, 220, 1313, 1144, 15487, 220, 1691, 1144, 15487, 220, 508, 1144, 15487, 220, 777, 1144, 15487, 220, 972, 1144, 15487, 220, 1114, 1144, 15487, 220, 845, 1144, 15487, 220, 868, 1144, 15487, 220, 975, 1144, 15487, 220, 103